Well, if your kitten eats something, *you* aren't charged for it. In fact,
if your pet picks something up, and takes it outside, even then you won't
be charged for it: it's (un)legally yours.

Mimics are a different problem. With a low level character, you should try
to avoid exposing them. Which means *not* moving onto the space they're
on.

What I usually do is go into a shop accompanied by my pet, and *only* step
on items that my pet steps on. Drop these items near the door (they're
guaranteed non-cursed). I don't step on spaces that my pet won't step on:
these contain either cursed items or mimics.

And when I do identify a mimic by some means, I line myself up so that I
can use attack spells without breaking something. An easy way to avoid
this, of course, is *not* to use force bolt or a wand of striking, but,
say, magic missile (spell or wand) instead. These and the other attack
spells and wands *don't* break potions.

